CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17 --object-bits 12 --unwind 10 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ assigned prefix: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Fixed 2026-07-20: value_set_dereference lowers an offset-0 dereference
whose type is a struct PREFIX of the object's type to the base
SUBOBJECT (member selection) instead of a struct value typecast the
bit-blaster would havoc.  The desc keeps "^warning: ignoring" forbidden
as the soundness gate.
